  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Retailer Hugo Mann made home delivery part of the appeal of his furniture business. Its red lorries carried his name through the streets while taking purchases to customers. The service helped his Karlsruhe store grow, and branches followed in other German cities.\n\nHe also employed designer Jürgen Döhmann to give his expanding shops a recognisable appearance. Döhmann coordinated logos, signs, colours and interiors, extending the same identity from advertising to directions inside the stores. At Wertkauf, industrial shelving doubled as storage above customers' reach, reducing the space needed for separate warehouses and making replenishment easier. Colour-coded departments helped shoppers navigate the large halls.",
    "html": "<p>Retailer Hugo Mann made home delivery part of the appeal of his furniture business. Its red lorries carried his name through the streets while taking purchases to customers. The service helped his Karlsruhe store grow, and branches followed in other German cities.</p>\r\n<p>He also employed designer Jürgen Döhmann to give his expanding shops a recognisable appearance. Döhmann coordinated logos, signs, colours and interiors, extending the same identity from advertising to directions inside the stores. At Wertkauf, industrial shelving doubled as storage above customers' reach, reducing the space needed for separate warehouses and making replenishment easier. Colour-coded departments helped shoppers navigate the large halls.</p>\r\n",
